course: dictionary
lesson: 14892
title: Thinking again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To reconsider something means to think about it again, and maybe change your mind. The start of the word, re-, means again, and consider means to think about something carefully. «Ben chose the red bike, but after he saw the blue one, he decided to reconsider.» Ben thought again about his choice.
explain: You can also reconsider a plan or an answer. «The teacher asked the class to reconsider their plan for the science fair, because the volcano would not fit on the table.» The class looked at the plan again and thought about how to change it.
explain: Reconsider is a verb, so it changes its ending: reconsiders, reconsidered, reconsidering. A good check is to swap in think again about. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Reconsider means to think again about a decision or opinion, and possibly change it.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so reconsider means to consider again.
fact: «Please reconsider!» is a way of asking someone to think again before they decide.
fact: In maths, you might reconsider an answer that looks wrong, and check your working again.
fact: In a formal sense, to reconsider a case or plan means to look at it again.
exercise: «Please reconsider!» What is the speaker asking you to do? | Stop talking for ever | *Think again about your decision | Clear your plate and go to bed | Buy a new coat
exercise: Ruby wrote 45 for 6 times 7, but it looked wrong. What should she do? | Ignore it and move on to the next question | *Reconsider the answer and check her working again | Ask someone else to write it for her | Write the answer in bigger letters
exercise: «The council decided to reconsider the plan for the new park.» What does reconsider mean here? | Lose the plan so nobody can see it | Cancel the park for ever | Build the park straight away without looking again | *Look at the plan again and maybe change it
test: «She asked her dad to reconsider the decision about her bedtime.» What does reconsider mean here? | Tell him the decision was silly and leave | *Ask him to think again about it | Go to bed without asking | Shout at him until he gives in
test: Which word means nearly the same as reconsider? | Forget | Hurry | *Rethink | Sleep
exam: After hearing the new facts, the scientist decided to ______ her theory. | forget | celebrate | sing | *reconsider
